data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The repo is empty except for .git. I need to create the design and then dispatch to developer.\n\nBut first I need to understand the codesweep design system. The developer brief says to install @codesweep-ai/ui. But as orchestrator, I just need to design using the components available. I should probably check if the package is already installed somewhere or if I can inspect it. Actually, I don't need to install it myself. I just need to write DESIGN.md naming design system components.\n\nBut to write a good design, I should know what's in the catalog. The mission says \"The package ships a `catalog.json` naming everything else it offers.\" Let me see if I can inspect the package somewhere. Maybe it's available via npm. But since this is a sandbox, maybe I can install it in a temp location or check if there's a local copy.\n\nActually, I should design using the known components: Header, Footer, Button, AppShell, and colour tokens. The catalog might have more, but the design can be simple. Let me check if the package exists in npm or if I can install it locally to inspect catalog.json.\n\nActually, I think I should create a minimal design that uses these components. But to make informed choices, I should look at the catalog. Let me try installing the package in a temp dir to inspect it.\n\nBut wait - the developer brief says the orchestrator pushes design first. The developer will then install @codesweep-ai/ui. As orchestrator, I don't necessarily need to install it, but it would help to know the tokens and components.\n\nLet me try to install it in /tmp to inspect catalog.json and tokens."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789958834,"id":"chatcmpl-6b902e5208c24bb3acba8d742cdfdf01","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

